    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0300" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1385.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Group to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We beg to enclose herewith, for your
                    information and files, a copy of a letter addressed to us by his excellency
                    Chang Yin Tang, the Chinese Minister in Washington, together with a copy of our
                    reply of to-day, regarding the currency loan.</p>
                <p>Also we send you herewith a copy of a cable received to-day from Messrs. Morgan,
                    Grenfell &amp; Co., a copy of our reply to this message, quoting our cable to
                    Mr. F. H. McKnight, in Peking, a copy of which is also enclosed.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard Straight</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>






